 ## Overview
-Slice Filling with BFS Propagation extends simple slice filling by propagating filled voxels to adjacent neighbors within the slice plane using a Breadth-First Search (BFS) if the neighbor is also empty in both the main voxel grid and the current buffer. It sets bits in a buffer for empty space until it hits an existing solid voxel, then stops that direction. It differs from [Slice Filling (Simple)](1691-slice-filling-simple.md) by using BFS to fill connected empty regions in the 2D slice plane rather than just scanning linearly from the edges.
+Slice Filling with BFS Propagation extends simple slice filling by propagating filled voxels to adjacent neighbors within the slice plane using a Breadth-First Search (BFS) if the neighbor is also empty in both the main voxel grid and the current buffer [S1]. It sets bits in a buffer for empty space until it hits an existing solid voxel, then stops that direction [S1]. It differs from [Slice Filling (Simple)](1691-slice-filling-simple.md) by using BFS to fill connected empty regions in the 2D slice plane rather than just scanning linearly from the edges [S1].
 
