+### BFS Light Propagation
+A breadth-first search flood-fill algorithm that propagates light levels across a padded voxel chunk, attenuating by 1 per step through non-opaque blocks [S2]. Initialize a queue and seed it with all blocks where `propagated_light > 0` [S2]. Define 6D neighbor strides for the padded chunk: $[1, -1, \text{PADDED}, -\text{PADDED}, \text{PADDED} \times \text{PADDED}, -\text{PADDED} \times \text{PADDED}]$ [S2]. While queue is not empty, pop `(idx, level)` [S2]. If `level <= 1`, skip [S2]. Compute `new_level = level - 1` [S2]. Iterate over strides to find neighbor index `ni` [S2]. Skip if `ni` out of bounds [S2]. Light attenuation is 1 level per step (`new_level = level - 1`) [S2]. Propagation condition: Light only propagates through non-opaque blocks (`is_opaque()` returns false) [S2].
